<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banu Umayya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Banu Umayya was a powerful clan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a> tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>. The third <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, Uthman, belonged to it, and his favouring of kinsmen in appointments caused discontent that contributed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>'s crisis. A member of the clan, Mu'awiya, founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> in 661.</p></div>
